pySMESH: an SMDS mesh frees its cell links with its grid (SMESH V9_16_0).

Defect: every mesh whose inverse-element links were built leaks them when it is destroyed or
cleared. The links hold one list of cells per node, so the leak grows with the mesh.

Symptom: 20 computes of a 2 x 2 x 2 box at spacing 0.1, Cartesian_3D with viscous layers on
every face, each in a fresh mesh that is then closed. With the offset mesh and the offset
makers freed (StdMeshers_Cartesian_3D_offset_mesh_leak.patch,
StdMeshers_Cartesian_VL_offset_makers_leak.patch), the private bytes still grew by 0.90 MB per
compute (5.0 MB at spacing 0.05), against 0.10 MB with no layers. A bisection build put all of
it on the first SMDS_Mesh::FindElement of the layer step (setBnd2Sub), which builds the links
of the target mesh.

Root cause: since VTK 9.0, vtkUnstructuredGrid::Links is a vtkSmartPointer. The raw-pointer
code of SMDS_UnstructuredGrid::BuildLinks (SMDS_UnstructuredGrid.cxx:1062-1076) assigns
New() to it, which the smart pointer registers, then adds Register(this) and Delete(). That
leaves two references with one owner: the grid's destructor, vtkUnstructuredGrid::Initialize
(SMDS_Mesh::Clear) and a later assignment release only one. DeleteLinks (:1078-1086) calls
UnRegister before it clears the pointer, which is right only for that doubled count.

Change, in SMDS_UnstructuredGrid.cxx only: BuildLinks makes the links with
vtkSmartPointer::New and assigns them, so the grid holds exactly one reference; DeleteLinks
clears the smart pointer.

Not changed: how the links are built, read and updated, and every mesh.
diff --git a/src/SMDS/SMDS_UnstructuredGrid.cxx b/src/SMDS/SMDS_UnstructuredGrid.cxx
--- a/src/SMDS/SMDS_UnstructuredGrid.cxx
+++ b/src/SMDS/SMDS_UnstructuredGrid.cxx
@@ -1061,28 +1061,20 @@
 
 void SMDS_UnstructuredGrid::BuildLinks()
 {
-  // Remove the old links if they are already built
-  if (this->Links)
-  {
-    this->Links->UnRegister(this);
-  }
-
-  SMDS_CellLinks* links;
-  this->Links = links = SMDS_CellLinks::New();
-  (static_cast< vtkCellLinks *>(this->Links.GetPointer()))->Allocate(this->GetNumberOfPoints());
-  this->Links->Register(this);
+  // pySMESH: Links is a vtkSmartPointer (VTK 9), and it holds the one reference the grid
+  // owns. The Register/UnRegister/Delete calls of the raw-pointer code left a second
+  // reference, so the last links of every grid outlived it. Assigning the new links
+  // releases the old ones.
+  vtkSmartPointer< SMDS_CellLinks > links = vtkSmartPointer< SMDS_CellLinks >::New();
+  this->Links = links;
+  (static_cast< vtkCellLinks *>(links.GetPointer()))->Allocate(this->GetNumberOfPoints());
   links->BuildLinks(this, this->Connectivity,this->GetCellTypesArray() );
-  this->Links->Delete();
 }
 
 void SMDS_UnstructuredGrid::DeleteLinks()
 {
-  // Remove the old links if they are already built
-  if (this->Links)
-  {
-    this->Links->UnRegister(this);
-    this->Links = NULL;
-  }
+  // pySMESH: the smart pointer releases the grid's one reference (see BuildLinks)
+  this->Links = nullptr;
 }
 SMDS_CellLinks* SMDS_UnstructuredGrid::GetLinks()
 {
